  "request_text": "Build a greenfield Python package named 'tokenizer_lite'. It is a small, self-contained text token-counting library with a CLI. Create exactly these four files:\n1. 'tokenizer_lite/__init__.py' - exports TokenizerLite and count_tokens.\n2. 'tokenizer_lite/core.py' - defines class TokenizerLite with methods count(text), count_words(text), and a module-level function count_tokens(text) that returns a dict with keys 'tokens', 'characters' and 'words'. Splitting must be whitespace based, must treat consecutive whitespace as one separator, and must return zeros for empty or whitespace-only input.\n3. 'tokenizer_lite/cli.py' - a 'main()' function with an argparse parser accepting one positional 'text' argument, printing 'tokens=<n> characters=<n> words=<n>' and returning exit code 0.\n4. 'test_tokenizer_lite.py' - pytest tests covering: empty string, whitespace-only string, single word, multiple words, and character count.\nAlso create 'README.md' with a title line, an Overview section and a Usage section. All code must be plain Python 3 with no third-party dependencies except pytest for the tests.",
